# walkr — Real Sports boost control

Look up a Real Sports App username, see their cards that are playing today, and
get a suggested booster for each unboosted card.

Deployed on Vercel → https://walkr.vercel.app (name was taken; pick a free
subdomain when you import — e.g. `walkr-real`).

## How it works

The Real Sports App has no public API. The official web app
(`web.realapp.com`) talks to a private JSON API from your logged-in browser
session. walkr sits server-side in front of that API:

```
enter username
  → /searchusers?query=            find the user's id (e.g. "R37MWQgJ")
  → /userpasses/{id}/passes?sport= full card collection
  → /home/{sport}/boostcontrol     cards owned that play today (+ boost state)
  → /userpassboostercards/...      booster inventory for that account
  → suggest-best-booster           highest rarity in stock → highest boost value
```

## Auth — you must set one of these

Real requires an authenticated session for these endpoints. All values live in
your browser after logging in at web.realapp.com (DevTools → Application →
Local Storage, or copy the `real-*` request headers from any Network request).
Two supported modes:

### Mode A — real-* headers (preferred; same as real-deal-tracker)

```
REAL_AUTH_INFO="<userId>!<deviceId>!<token>"   # localStorage key real-auth-info
REAL_SESSION_TOKEN="<token>"                   # localStorage key real-session-token
REAL_DEVICE_TYPE=""      # real-device-type header   (optional, may be empty)
REAL_DEVICE_NAME=""      # real-device-name header   (optional)
REAL_DEVICE_UUID=""      # real-device-uuid header   (optional)
REAL_VERSION=""          # real-version header       (optional)
```

`REAL_AUTH_INFO` is the actual credential (`{userId}!{deviceId}!{token}`,
copied verbatim from localStorage). A fresh `real-request-token` is generated
per request with a faithful TS port of Real's Hashids encoder
(`salt="realwebapp"`, min_length 16) — verified 15/15 against the minified
bundle.

### Mode B — cookie

```
REAL_AUTH_COOKIE="<full Cookie header from a logged-in web.realapp.com request>"
```

## Important caveat

`boostcontrol` is scoped to the **logged-in account** whose session is in your
env vars. The dashboard shows the intersection of (that account's cards playing
today) and (the looked-up username's collection) — so it is fully correct for
your own username, and for other usernames it only shows cards you both own.

Only MLB is wired up so far. WNBA / CFB / NFL / NHL / FC tabs are placeholders —
each needs a one-line sport key + capture-verification of the same endpoints.

## Deploy

1. Push this folder to a GitHub repo.
2. vercel.com → Add New Project → import the repo (framework auto-detected: Next.js).
3. Settings → Environment Variables → paste the REAL_* values above.
4. Deploy. Set the project subdomain under Settings → Domains.

Local dev: `cp .env.example .env`, fill it in, then `npm run dev`.
